   "source": [
    "# 📖 Building Evaluators\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🎯 Learning Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Build LLM-as-Judge evaluators\n",
    "2. Create custom evaluators\n",
    "3. Chain evaluators together\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ⏱️ Time Estimate\n",
    "**~30 minutes**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type":="markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🧠 What Are Evaluators?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evaluators** are functions that check if agent output meets criteria.\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n",
    "│              EVALUATOR PATTERN                         │\n",
    "├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│  Input:  {run, reference, prediction}                   │\n",
    "│  Process: Check against criteria                       │\n",
    "│  Output: {key: value, ...}                            │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "│  Always returns:                                       │\n",
    "│  - feedback (explanation)                            │\n",
    "│  - score (numeric)                                   │\n",
    "│  - correction (optional fix)                          │\n",
    "│                                                         │\n",
    "└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "if \"OPENAI_API_KEY\" not in os.environ:\n",
    "    os.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"] = getpass.getpass(\"OpenAI Key: \")\n",
    "\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "client = OpenAI()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1️⃣ LLM-as-Judge Evaluator\n",
    "\n",
    "The most powerful approach - use an LLM to judge outputs:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def llm_judge_evaluator(input_query: str, reference: str, prediction: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Use LLM to judge if prediction is acceptable.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    judge_prompt = f\"\"\"Evaluate this AI response.\n",
    "\n",
    "Query: {input_query}\n",
    "Reference Answer: {reference}\n",
    "AI Response: {prediction}\n",
    "\n",
    "Is the AI response acceptable? Consider:\n",
    "1. Is the answer correct?\n",
    "2. Is it complete?\n",
    "3. Is it helpful?\n",
    "\n",
    "Respond with:\n",
    "SCORE: 0-100\n",
    "FEEDBACK: Brief explanation\n",
    "PASSED: true/false\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n",
    "        model=\"gpt-4o-mini\",\n",
    "        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": judge_prompt}]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    result_text = response.choices[0].message.content\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Parse result (simplified)\n",
    "    score = 80 if \"SCORE:\" in result_text else 50\n",
    "    passed = \"PASSED: true\" in result_text.lower() or score >= 70\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"score\": score,\n",
    "        \"passed\": passed,\n",
    "        \"feedback\": result_text\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test it\n",
    "result = llm_judge_evaluator(\n",
    "    input_query=\"What is 2+2?\",\n",
    "    reference=\"4\",\n",
    "    prediction=\"The answer is 4.\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"📊 LLM Judge Result: {result}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2️⃣ Assertion-Based Evaluators\n",
    "\n",
    "Simple pass/fail checks:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def assert_contains(text: str, substring: str) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Assert response contains expected text.\"\"\"\n",
    "    passed = substring.lower() in text.lower()\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"passed\": passed,\n",
    "        \"feedback\": f\"Contains '{substring}': {passed}\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "def assert_no_hallucination(text: str, known_facts: list) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Check for hallucination markers.\"\"\"\n",
    "    uncertainty_phrases = [\"i'm not sure\", \"might be\", \"perhaps\", \"as far as I know\"]\n",
    "    has_uncertainty = any(phrase in text.lower() for phrase in uncertainty_phrases)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"passed\": not has_uncertainty,\n",
    "        \"has_uncertainty_markers\": has_uncertainty,\n",
    "        \"feedback\": \"Hallucination detected\" if has_uncertainty else \"Looks good\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test\n",
    "print(assert_contains(\"The capital is Paris\", \"Paris\"))\n",
    "print(assert_contains(\"The capital is London\", \"Paris\"))\n",
    "print(assert_no_hallucination(\"The capital is Paris\", [\"Paris\"]))\n",
    "print(assert_no_hallucination(\"The capital might be Paris\", []))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3️⃣ Trajectory Evaluators"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def eval_tool_usage(run: dict, expected_tools: list) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Check if expected tools were used.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    tool_calls = [tc[\"tool\"] for tc in run.get(\"tool_calls\", [])]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Check each expected tool\n",
    "    missing_tools = [t for t in expected_tools if t not in tool_calls]\n",
    "    extra_tools = [t for t in tool_calls if t not in expected_tools]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    passed = len(missing_tools) == 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"passed\": passed,\n",
    "        \"expected_tools\": expected_tools,\n",
    "        \"actual_tools\": tool_calls,\n",
    "        \"missing\": missing_tools,\n",
    "        \"extra\": extra_tools,\n",
    "        \"feedback\": f\"Used {len(tool_calls)} tools\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test\n",
    "run = {\"tool_calls\": [{\"tool\": \"web_search\"}, {\"tool\": \"llm\"}]}\n",
    "print(eval_tool_usage(run, [\"web_search\"]))\n",
    "print(eval_tool_usage(run, [\"web_search\", \"calculator\"]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🔗 Chaining Evaluators"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_evaluators(input_query: str, reference: str, prediction: str, run: dict) -> dict:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run multiple evaluators and combine.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    results = []\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 1. LLM Judge\n",
    "    judge_result = llm_judge_evaluator(input_query, reference, prediction)\n",
    "    results.append((\"llm_judge\", judge_result))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Contains check\n",
    "    contains_result = assert_contains(prediction, reference)\n",
    "    results.append((\"contains\", contains_result))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 3. No hallucination\n",
    "    hallucination_result = assert_no_hallucination(prediction, [])\n",
    "    results.append((\"hallucination\", hallucination_result))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Combine\n",
    "    all_passed = all(r[1][\"passed\"] for r in results)\n",
    "    avg_score = sum(r[1].get(\"score\", 100) for r in results) / len(results)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"overall_passed\": all_passed,\n",
    "        \"score\": avg_score,\n",
    "        \"evaluators\": {name: res for name, res in results}\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test\n",
    "result = run_evaluators(\n",
    "    input_query=\"What is Python?\",\n",
    "    reference=\"Python is a programming language\",\n",
    "    prediction=\"Python is a programming language.\",\n",
    "    run={}\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"📊 Combined Eval: {result['overall_passed']}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type":="markdown",
